## Why This Is Asked
- Tests practical concurrency design under load with backpressure and shutdown semantics. **Expects** concrete data structures and synchronization choices.

## Key Concepts
- **Thread-safety**, **bounded buffers**, and **backpressure**
- Correct handling of spurious wakeups
- Liveness guarantees and clean shutdown

## Code Example

```java
class BoundedMPMCQueue<T> {
  private final Object[] buf; private int head=0, tail=0, count=0;
  private final ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();
  private final Condition notFull = lock.newCondition();
  private final Condition notEmpty = lock.newCondition();
  private volatile boolean shutdown = false;

  public BoundedMPMCQueue(int capacity){ buf = new Object[capacity]; }

  public void enqueue(T item) throws InterruptedException {
    lock.lock();
    try {
      while (count == buf.length && !shutdown) notFull.await();
      if (shutdown) throw new InterruptedException();
      buf[tail] = item; tail = (tail+1) % buf.length; count++;
      notEmpty.signalAll();
    } finally { lock.unlock(); }
  }

  public T dequeue() throws InterruptedException {
    lock.lock();
    try {
      while (count == 0 && !shutdown) notEmpty.await();
      if (shutdown && count == 0) return null;
      @SuppressWarnings("unchecked") T item = (T) buf[head]; buf[head] = null; head = (head+1) % buf.length; count--;
      notFull.signalAll();
      return item;
    } finally { lock.unlock(); }
  }

  public void shutdown() {
    lock.lock(); try { shutdown = true; notFull.signalAll(); notEmpty.signalAll(); } finally { lock.unlock(); }
  }
}
```

